WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:06.259
From a world-ending apocalypse to yet more
timeline jumps and shenanigans, the third

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:11.230
season of The Umbrella Academy ends on a huge
cliffhanger and a big reveal about Reginald

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.230
Hargreaves.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.680
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining everything you need

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.240
to know about the ending of Season 3, what
the deal was that Allison made, and why we're

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.740
likely getting doppelgangers in Season 4!

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.820
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:30.930
When the Umbrella Academy arrived back in
2019 to find themselves replaced by the Sparrows,

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:35.870
on the same day they arrived, a Kugelblitz,
a type of black hole, appeared in the basement

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.170
of the Sparrow Academy.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.300
You see, when they travelled back to the 60s
they inadvertently transferred powers to a

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.050
young Harlan, who as he grew up found himself
connected to other powered people.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:51.929
When his mother, Sissy, died on the 1st of
October 1989, it was the same day the Umbrella

00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:53.660
Academy's mothers were due to give birth.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:58.880
As the super-babies grew inside them, Harlan
sensed their pain and when this combined with

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.480
his grief over Sissy's death, he accidentally
killed them, preventing the Umbrella Academy

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.159
team from ever being born.

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:10.000
So, when the gang arrive in this new timeline,
they shouldn't actually exist, and this creates

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.070
a version of the grandfather paradox.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.070
A paradox?

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.431
You mean one of those things that could destroy
the universe?

00:01:15.431 --> 00:01:20.020
The threat the Kugelblitz poses to the entire
cosmos now explains just why the Commission

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:24.370
was so alarmed when they found out about Harlan's
powers in the second season.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.700
I've never seen anything like this.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.500
The anomaly is off the charts.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.770
The Kugelblitz is unstoppable without going
back in time to prevent their mothers being

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:36.320
killed, which is impossible as the only two
available Commission briefcases are broken.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.950
The only remedy lies in the Hotel Oblivion.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:44.299
The Oblivion is located in an alternate dimension,
a nod to how the hotel in the comics it exists

00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:48.789
in a pocket dimension and was used by Hargreaves
as a prison for villains.

00:01:48.789 --> 00:01:52.850
And the numerous cockroaches that keep popping
up are a reference to how the critters were

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.500
served to the prisoners at the hotel in the
comics.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.350
In the TV show, the Oblivion contains a machine
that can rebuild the universe should it ever

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.390
be destroyed.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:06.580
The machine is activated by the seven bells,
which it turns out are seven of the surviving

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:07.580
team.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:12.010
And when they stand on the stars on the floor
of the hotel's lobby, they create the sigil,

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.780
which unlocks the machine.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.340
The Oblivion then reveals that it's basically
an illusion for a Matrix-like machine that

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.860
controls the reality of the world.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:26.010
Another cool detail here is the hotel floor
tiling that creates an optical illusion, another

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:30.660
pointer to the Hotel Oblivion's perception
and reality-altering powers.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:35.450
The machine then begins to pull sparks of
light out of the seven members of the team,

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.940
something that Allison protests as it appears
to be about to kill them.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:42.590
The particles inside their bodies are the
only things that fuel the machine.

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:46.950
Now, these flecks of lights are the ones that
Hargreaves released a long time ago back on

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:47.950
his home world.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:53.180
And the opening scene of Season 3 confirmed
that they are the thing that miraculously

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:58.440
impregnated numerous women around the world
who, on the same day, all gave birth to super-powered

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.470
children.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.470
And they're also the same lights that transferred
to Harlan in Season 2 to give him his powers.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:04.209
And this makes me think it was part of Hargreaves'
plan to use humans as vessels for transferring

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:08.849
the magical lights from his home world, eventually
all the way to the Hotel Oblivion, where he

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:13.519
could then extract them to power up the engine
that would recreate the cosmos.

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:17.629
With access to the machine, I think he then
programmed the rebirth of the universe in

00:03:17.629 --> 00:03:21.760
a way that would prevent the apocalypse on
his home planet and the death of his wife.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:26.090
After all, remember that he said:
I've seen worlds end in ways that would knock

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:27.090
your socks off.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:28.459
But you never forget your first.

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:29.459
Your home.

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:30.459
Your original sin.

00:03:30.459 --> 00:03:34.060
You never stop wondering,
"Did I do enough to save the people I loved?"

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.060
Did you?

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.749
No, but I was hoping you children could help
me out with that.

00:03:37.749 --> 00:03:43.300
Season 3 also revealed that bringing his wife
back to life has been a huge driving force

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:47.630
for Hargreaves, when we discover that he was
keeping her body cryogenically frozen in a

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:49.189
container on the moon.

00:03:49.189 --> 00:03:54.110
He even sent Luther there for four years on
an unexplained mission to keep her safe.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:56.319
You wasted my life on the moon, and for what?

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.930
I left you to guard the most precious thing
in the universe.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:03.530
I even suspect that Hargreaves himself may
have cycled through various loops in time

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:08.079
in order to figure out what combination of
events would eventually lead him to discover

00:04:08.079 --> 00:04:11.069
the key to fixing the universe in his favour.

00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:16.060
In Season 1's flashback to Hargreaves arrival
in America, we can see from the immigration

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:18.160
stamp that this was 1928.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:24.830
But in Season 3, we discover Hargreaves was
already on Earth in 1918 looking for the portal

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.270
to the alternate dimension.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:32.320
Even after uncovering the portal, his attempts
to get safe access inside were thwarted by

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:37.080
the Guardians protecting the other side,
and when he saw how a group of trained soldiers

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.751
were so easily defeated by the samurai warriors,
that might have led him to the idea that he

00:04:41.751 --> 00:04:45.730
needed a group of extraordinary, super-powered
individuals for the task.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:50.650
For that, he might have gone back again in
time to release the magical lights, and since

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:55.400
then he's gone through many cycles of different
super-babies and children until finding the

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.610
seven who would become the seven bells.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:03.580
Another big clue to Hargreaves' secret time
travel shenanigans is the fact there's a Televator

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:06.500
sign hidden in the basement of the Sparrow
Academy.

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:12.020
In the comics, the Televator is a contraption
that can travel across space, time and dimensions,

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:16.790
and in the Season-2 60s timeline we saw that
Hargreaves had blueprints in his office for

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.170
building a Televator.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:23.020
As he said to Five, he's witnessed numerous
apocalypses before, so perhaps that's how

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:26.700
he's escaped through time and space on several
occasions.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:31.730
And if you like this theory or this video
so far, hit that like button, I really appreciate

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:32.730
it.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:37.290
But what was the deal Allison made with Reginald
on the night of Luther and Sloane's wedding?

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:42.060
I think she offered to unite her side of the
family by reconciling with them the following

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:46.460
day then trying to convince them to join Hargreaves'
mission to the Oblivion.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:52.030
Although that didn't exactly work, she had
tried, and so once on the other side, in return,

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:56.630
perhaps out of some slight empathy for her
given his mission was also to recover his

00:05:56.630 --> 00:06:01.910
lost love, Hargreaves programmed the new universe
so that she could have the two cherished things

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:07.390
she'd lost in all the timeline changes:
her daughter Claire from 2019, and her husband

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:08.860
Ray from the 60s.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:09.860
I'm almost done.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:12.560
And when I am, you and I will get what we
came here for.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:18.050
This new universe is Allison's idealised world
where her mistakes and problems from the previous

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:19.910
two seasons are now gone.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:24.700
In Season 1, after Allison's husband Patrick
found her using her powers on their daughter,

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:27.810
he divorced her and took custody of Claire.

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:32.240
And in Season 2, she had to leave her husband
Ray, who she'd fallen in love with, so that

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.270
she could travel back to the future.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:39.110
Now, in this new and improved timeline, Allison
has managed to get the two people she loves

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:41.650
from different times in one place.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:45.950
Reginald too got what he was finally after
too and created a world where not only is

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:50.480
his wife Abigail still alive, but once more
he's a billionaire, with what looks like an

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:52.920
even bigger business empire this time.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:58.180
As for Allison's siblings, they emerge in
the new world dramatically changed.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:02.930
Luther has lost his simian body, Diego's fingers
that were sliced off by one of the Guardians

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:06.370
have returned and Five also has both his arms.

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:09.700
The wrinkle, however, is that they don't have
their powers any more:

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:10.700
I can't blink.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:15.091
Now, it's possible that they lost their abilities
when the particles were extracted out of them

00:07:15.091 --> 00:07:20.240
by the Oblivion's world-reset machine, which
would also mean that Allison would still have

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:26.100
her powers, but it doesn't totally explain
how Luther is 100% human again, or how Diego's

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.820
fingers and Five's arm have returned.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:33.370
And thanks to this cryptic final scene where
we see Ben riding the subway to a stop in

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:38.700
the financial district of Seoul, Korea, I
think that in Season 4, we'll be seeing doppelgangers.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:43.390
The clues are subtle but notice how this Ben
doesn't have a scar on his face implying that

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:46.940
it isn't Sparrow Ben, plus his hairstyle is
different.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:51.910
The scene is also a call-back to the opening
scene of Season 3 where a young Korean girl

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:56.590
on the subway is impregnated by the magical
lights and gives birth immediately.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:08:00.860
Whether Ben was born that way in this new
timeline, we don't yet know, and therefore

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.630
we can't be sure whether this Ben has any
powers.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:08.130
After all, Hargreaves may well have decided
that he didn't need to release any magic lights

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.660
this time after the adjustments he'd made
to the timeline with the machine at the Oblivion.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:17.620
I think this final scene is also pointing
to the idea that in Season 4, we'll be getting

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:21.490
doppelgangers for the other Umbrella Academy
members as well.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:25.640
Remember how at the start of Season 3, there
was specific mention by Five of how they could

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:29.010
expect to meet a copy of themselves in the
new timeline.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:32.940
Dad didn't adopt us as babies, but those babies
still existed here.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:36.100
Odds are, we each have identical versions
of ourselves.

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.100
Our doppelgängers!

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.500
Doppels probably aren't even in the same time
zone as us.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:44.120
That never happened in Season 3 because the
Umbrellas' mothers all died before they gave

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:49.400
birth, but I think the point of Five bringing
up the subject was to set up the idea for

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:50.400
Season 4.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:53.950
In other words, it's basically Chekov's Doppelgangers.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:58.460
If the Umbrella gang's powers do return and
the doppels also have powers, it could be

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:03.030
fun if they get into an argument or fight
with themselves, much like Five did in Season

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:04.110
2.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:08.450
Another theory I have about how the team might
regain their powers is with the help of a

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:09.450
Televator.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:13.890
As I mentioned earlier, this machine can not
only travel through time and space, but also

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:18.530
between dimensions, meaning they could try
and return to their old universe before it

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:22.920
was Kugelblitzed, get back their old powers
and then stop the apocalypse.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:27.640
A hint at this idea might be the fact that
they came into this new universe via the door

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.880
of an elevator from the Hotel Oblivion.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:35.250
So, could that elevator itself be a secret
Televator with a hidden activation switch?

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:40.710
Also to be revealed in Season 4 is why Sloane
is missing in the final scene, given she was

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:43.660
with the others at the moment Allison pressed
the button?

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:47.910
I don't think she's been written out of the
show, especially given that Luther has run

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:52.790
off looking for her, and I suspect the opening
scene of her reading a travel book with the

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:57.750
Leaning Tower of Pisa on the cover is a hint
that she's ended up somewhere else, perhaps

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:58.750
Italy.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:01.560
And we know when Sloane was with Luther, she
talked about wanting to get away.

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:05.680
I know there are better places out there in
the world, and one day, I want to see them

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:06.680
all.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:10.770
I'm also curious to see what happens with
Lila and Diego, especially as she's pregnant,

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:13.240
whether they'll end up having a super-baby?

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:16.790
Another question is how is Luther back at
all, given he'd died?

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:21.500
Did the ghostly spirit of him that Klaus conjured
up at the Oblivion mean he could be reborn

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:23.130
into the new world?

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:27.470
Klaus chases after Luther, so there's something
between the two of them that will be explained

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:28.940
in Season 4.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:33.430
In fact, there were some neat clues very early
on that predicted how both Klaus and Luther

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:38.370
would end up together in the afterlife, something
I explain in my Season 3 easter eggs and things

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.810
you missed video, which I'll be uploading
next.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:43.770
I'll add a link here and in the description
as soon as it's ready.

